---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/jsonld';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Audio MCP Server — 8 Local FFmpeg Tools';
const description =
  'Run trim, join, convert, fade, and loudness on files already on your computer. Eight ffmpeg tools over stdio; an MP3 is encoded once.';
const pageUrl = new URL('/mcp', SITE.url).href;
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Does this server upload my file?',
    a: 'No upload to this site. The process is stdio on your computer, and ffmpeg reads the path you pass. The chat app still sees that path and the arguments. A browser tool is different: the file stays inside the tab.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to the audio quality?',
    a: 'MP3, M4A, and OGG are encoded once. The bitrate choices are 64, 96, 128, 192, 256, and 320 kbps, and the default is 192. WAV is 16-bit PCM. FLAC is lossless. Joined files are 44100 Hz stereo. Tag writes copy the audio and write ID3v2.3. Normalize is one loudnorm pass at -16 LUFS, -1.5 dBTP, and LRA 11.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What can it not do?',
    a: 'No waveform, no microphone, no transcription, and no cover art. It does not fetch a video from a link. A single call is stopped after 15 minutes. Pitch, recording, transcription, and a spectrogram stay on the browser pages.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is this different from the browser tools?',
    a: 'The browser tools use the Web Audio API and need no install. This server calls ffmpeg. Tempo here is 0.5× to 2×. The tempo page is 0.75× to 1.25×. Fade here is 0 to 30 seconds. The fade page is 0 to 5 seconds. Normalize here is loudnorm. The normalize page moves the peak to about -0.2 dB.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it run on a phone?',
    a: 'No. It needs Node.js 18 or newer, ffmpeg, and a desktop client that speaks MCP, such as Claude Desktop or Cursor. A phone browser cannot start a stdio server.',
  },
];
const install = `cd free-audio-editor-mcp
npm install`;
const clientConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "audio": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/free-audio-editor-mcp/index.js"]
    }
  }
}`;
const zipUrl = new URL('/free-audio-editor-mcp.zip', SITE.url).href;
const agentPrompt = `Install the Audio MCP server from Free Audio Editor on this computer, then register it with this chat client. Do the work. Do not only print the steps.

1. Download ${zipUrl} and unzip it so the folder is exactly ~/free-audio-editor-mcp on macOS or Linux, or %USERPROFILE%\\free-audio-editor-mcp on Windows. That folder must stay. Do not use a temp directory. If the folder is already there, replace the files from this zip and continue. Do not touch anything outside that folder.
2. In that folder, run npm install. Node.js must be 18 or newer. This package is not on npm. Do not use npx. Do not publish it.
3. ffmpeg and ffprobe must be installed. If the command is missing: macOS, brew install ffmpeg. Windows, winget install FFmpeg. Debian and Ubuntu, sudo apt install ffmpeg.
4. In that folder, run node check.js. If it prints FAIL, stop and fix that before writing a config.
5. Register one server named audio. Merge it into the existing JSON and keep every other mcpServers entry. Create the file and parent directories if they are missing.
   command: node. If this app does not inherit the shell PATH, use the absolute path of the node binary instead.
   args: one item, the absolute path of free-audio-editor-mcp/index.js.
   If this app will not see ffmpeg on PATH, add env FFMPEG_PATH and FFPROBE_PATH with the absolute binaries.
   Shape:
   { "mcpServers": { "audio": { "command": "node", "args": ["/ABSOLUTE/PATH/free-audio-editor-mcp/index.js"] } } }
6. Write the file for the app you are running in. Cursor, for every project: ~/.cursor/mcp.json on macOS and Linux, %USERPROFILE%\\.cursor\\mcp.json on Windows. Claude Desktop: ~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json on macOS, %APPDATA%\\Claude\\claude_desktop_config.json on Windows. On Linux, if you are in Claude Desktop, edit the config file that app already uses. Do not invent a new path. If you cannot tell which app this is, write the Cursor file and the Claude Desktop file for this operating system.
7. Do not leave index.js running. The client starts it over stdio.
8. Reply with the absolute path you configured, the config file you wrote, and tell me to quit and reopen this app.

The tools are audio_trim, audio_join, audio_convert, audio_normalize, audio_fade, audio_extract, audio_tags, and audio_tempo. Each one calls ffmpeg on a file already on this computer. Nothing is uploaded to ${SITE.url}.`;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: 'Audio MCP Server',
    description,
    url: pageUrl,
    downloadUrl: new URL('/free-audio-editor-mcp.zip', SITE.url).href,
    applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'macOS, Windows, Linux',
    softwareRequirements: 'Node.js 18 or newer, ffmpeg and ffprobe on PATH',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    featureList: [
      'audio_trim',
      'audio_join',
      'audio_convert',
      'audio_normalize',
      'audio_fade',
      'audio_extract',
      'audio_tags',
      'audio_tempo',
    ],
  },
  faqSchema(faqs, 'en'),
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Audio MCP Server', path: '/mcp' },
  ]),
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/mcp" locale="en" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="container-page py-14">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-xs">
      <a href="/" class="text-ink3 hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5 text-ink3">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink2" aria-current="page">Audio MCP Server</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Audio MCP Server</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink2">
      Eight tools for Claude Desktop and Cursor. Each one calls ffmpeg on a file already on your computer.
      This site never receives the file. There is no account. The chat app still sees the path and the arguments.
    </p>

    <div class="guide-prose mt-2 min-w-0 max-w-[65ch] [&_code]:break-all">
      <h2>What you can run</h2>
      <p>
        The name in the first column is the tool the client calls. The browser page is the same job with no
        install. The engines differ: the browser uses the Web Audio API, and this server uses ffmpeg.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Tool</th>
              <th>On your computer</th>
              <th>In the browser</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_trim</code></td>
              <td>Start and end in seconds. WAV is decoded samples. MP3 is encoded once.</td>
              <td><a href="/audio-trimmer">Audio Trimmer</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_join</code></td>
              <td>2 to 20 files. Crossfade 0 to 5 seconds. Output is 44100 Hz stereo.</td>
              <td><a href="/audio-joiner">Audio Joiner</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_convert</code></td>
              <td>mp3, wav, flac, m4a, or ogg. Lossy rates are 64, 96, 128, 192, 256, or 320 kbps. Default 192.</td>
              <td><a href="/wav-to-mp3">WAV to MP3</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_normalize</code></td>
              <td>One loudnorm pass: -16 LUFS, -1.5 dBTP, LRA 11. Not a second measured pass.</td>
              <td><a href="/normalize-audio">Normalize Audio</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_fade</code></td>
              <td>Fade in and fade out, each from 0 to 30 seconds.</td>
              <td><a href="/fade-audio">Fade Audio</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_extract</code></td>
              <td>Soundtrack of a local video. A codec opens only if your ffmpeg build has that decoder.</td>
              <td><a href="/extract-audio">Extract Audio</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_tags</code></td>
              <td>Read, or write title, artist, album, date, genre, track, and comment. Audio is copied. ID3v2.3. No cover art.</td>
              <td><a href="/mp3-tag-editor">MP3 Tag Editor</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>audio_tempo</code></td>
              <td>0.5× to 2× with ffmpeg atempo. Pitch stays.</td>
              <td><a href="/tempo-changer">Tempo Changer</a></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Install</h2>
      <p>
        This server is not on npm. You need Node.js 18 or newer, plus ffmpeg and ffprobe on PATH.
      </p>
      <h3>Paste this to Claude or Cursor</h3>
      <p>
        Copy this and paste it into the chat. That client downloads the zip, installs it, and writes its own
        config. Quit and reopen the app when it says to.
      </p>
      <p>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-copy-prompt>
          <span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
        </button>
      </p>
      <pre id="mcp-agent-prompt" class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink">{agentPrompt}</pre>
      <h3>Or install it yourself</h3>
      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary download-mcp" href="/free-audio-editor-mcp.zip" download="free-audio-editor-mcp.zip">Download the server</a>
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink">{install}</pre>
      <p>Install ffmpeg if the command is missing:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>macOS: <code>brew install ffmpeg</code></li>
        <li>Windows: <code>winget install FFmpeg</code></li>
        <li>Debian and Ubuntu: <code>sudo apt install ffmpeg</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Claude Desktop reads <code>~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json</code> on macOS
        and <code>%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json</code> on Windows. Cursor reads
        <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>, or <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code> in a project. Same JSON either way.
        Replace the path with the <code>index.js</code> you just installed. Restart the client after saving.
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink">{clientConfig}</pre>
      <p>
        If the binary is not on PATH, set <code>FFMPEG_PATH</code> and <code>FFPROBE_PATH</code> in that config’s
        <code>env</code> block.
      </p>

      <h2>What this does not do</h2>
      <p>
        There is no waveform, no microphone, and no model download. Pitch stays on the
        <a href="/pitch-changer">pitch changer</a>. Recording stays on the
        <a href="/voice-recorder">voice recorder</a>. Transcription stays on
        <a href="/audio-to-text">audio to text</a>. A picture of the spectrum stays on the
        <a href="/spectrogram-generator">spectrogram generator</a>. Echo stays on
        <a href="/echo">echo</a>. The server does not read a video URL.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        ffmpeg runs on the machine where the client runs. Nothing is posted to {SITE.name}. The chat client still
        receives the path and the arguments, and that client may send the conversation to its own API. The
        <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> covers the browser tools, where the file stays in the tab.
      </p>

      <h2>When a call fails</h2>
      <p>The tool returns the sentence below. Fix that, then call it again.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>ffmpeg was not found on PATH. Install ffmpeg, then restart the client.</code>
          Install ffmpeg, or set <code>FFMPEG_PATH</code>, then restart.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>output must be a different file</code> — the output path is the same as an input. Pick a new name.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>fades (… + … s) are longer than the file</code> — shorten the fades. A fade cannot be longer than the file.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>inputs needs 2 to 20 files</code> — join starts at two files and stops at 20.
        </li>
        <li>A call that runs longer than 15 minutes is stopped.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Faq faqs={faqs} locale="en" />
</Base>

<style>
  .guide-prose a.download-mcp,
  .guide-prose a.download-mcp:hover {
    color: var(--color-on-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
<script>
  const copyPrompt = document.querySelector('[data-copy-prompt]');
  const promptSource = document.querySelector('#mcp-agent-prompt');
  if (copyPrompt instanceof HTMLButtonElement && promptSource) {
    const label = copyPrompt.querySelector('[data-copy-label]');
    const idle = label?.textContent ?? 'Copy';
    copyPrompt.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const text = promptSource.textContent ?? '';
      let ok = false;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        ok = true;
      } catch {
        try {
          const input = document.createElement('textarea');
          input.value = text;
          input.setAttribute('readonly', '');
          input.style.position = 'fixed';
          input.style.opacity = '0';
          document.body.append(input);
          input.select();
          ok = document.execCommand('copy');
          input.remove();
        } catch {
          ok = false;
        }
      }
      if (!ok) {
        const range = document.createRange();
        range.selectNodeContents(promptSource);
        const selection = getSelection();
        selection?.removeAllRanges();
        selection?.addRange(range);
      }
      if (!label) return;
      label.textContent = ok ? 'Copied' : 'Selected';
      window.setTimeout(() => {
        label.textContent = idle;
      }, 2000);
    });
  }
</script>
